```
let startIndex = 0;
let offset = 0;
```

3. Loop through the array and calculate the offset by comparing the current index with the target index.

```
for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
  if (i == elementIndex) {
    break;
  }

  if (i != elementIndex && array[i] != undefined) {
    offset++;
  }

  if (i == elementIndex) {
    break;
  }

  startIndex = i;
}
``
4. Calculate the offset by subtracting the starting index from the current index.

```
offset = Math.abs(startIndex - i);
```

5. If the target element is at the beginning of the array, the offset will be 0.

6. If the target element is not found, the offset will be the index of the last element in the array.

7. Return the calculated offset.

```
return offset;
```

